Subject: [PATCH 10/11] detect: opt-in rule_snapshots, so rule-layer candidates
 can be asked (EMERGENCE-Next)

detectors.rule_snapshots (optional, absent = false = the shipped candidate
source). A candidate the rule layer found but no detector alerted on gets a
snapshot from its rule hit: the first rule week at which a full detector
window fits, as_of that week's close, the rule's sites as supporting sites,
score 0, source 'rule'. Detector snapshots are untouched. The HQ bridge
publishes conclusions only under the detection run's recorded snapshot week,
so this keeps the provenance chain instead of synthesising questions at HQ.
Nothing new crosses a Boundary: the rule layer runs on HQ's existing weekly
cells.

Seed 0 (min_history 1, uncapped): true patterns asked inside their window
23 -> 35 (rare 3 -> 14); questions 84 -> 539; decoy questions 53 -> 97.
For the frozen track this is the root-cause report's rank 7 (founder's
decision on the candidate source); here it is a versioned research setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
